Z||000000||GT Bastard||07-30-2000||11:14 PM||||What's everyones take on heavy duty vs. stock replacement clutches? It looks like the ACT 4-puck clutch is going to be replaced during the 3.2 swap.  The race clutch is entertaining, but I'm not a real big fan of the harsh nature of it.  On the other hand, I don't want a cheap replacement that craps-out in a couple months.  A lot of people seem to think there isn't a big difference between stock vs. Heavy duty, but I'm undecided.  Anybody have suggestions or input? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||lowCG||07-31-2000||12:03 AM||||I've got a West Coast Fiero unit that's ten or so Kevlar pucks on a beefed-up stock disc,used with a Luk pressure plate,and it's real easy to drive around,yet requires some technique over a stock unit of course.||||reg||1
