Z||000003||1FST2M6||07-31-2000||01:34 PM||||if your really gunna pull it out of the car I'll buy it from you! We know it holds 300+lbft and will out last the other ones I've used..  let me know! <BR>Chris West swears by his stuff. and so do the drivers of the cars they are in...  the headers should be SWEET on a 3.2... i hope... <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||07-31-2000||01:47 PM||||Yeah, I'm really curious if the extra cubes will make better use of the headers...  Damn, you guys are vultures! hehe<P>10-puck kevlar clutch?  Sounds interesting.  I've heard that 6-pucks are pretty livable, but then I'd want to use a new pressure plate .  Hmmmmmm||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||07-31-2000||01:51 PM||||I don't race my 85SE v-6 but I do like to run it hard at times.  I installed a new OEM Borg Warner clutch ($109 for disk, pressure plate, throw out bearing, and pilot bearing) and am very pleased.  It engages smoothly with no chatter and holds very well.  Hard launches don't seem to bother it at all.  I've had it in around a year and have put about 6000 miles on it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||07-31-2000||07:13 PM||||a Kevlar unit should be ok... obviously replace the pressure plate and bearing and resurface the Flywheel... it hasn't ever been turned.. bought it BRAND SPANKIN new, sprayed it with Brake cleaner wiped it off and put it back together.. (you should have the recipt for that) the Springs in the center hub are more for Harmonics than chatter. (sprung and unsprung hub clutches)the friction materials are the culprits that cause chatter. But the unsprung units have NOTHING to shoot out and wedge in to the pressure plate and make loud noises and stop the car... Clutchnet makes unsprung organic and kevlar discs. they will slip (engage more smoothly) for street driving than the Ceramic that is in the car now. and won't fail with any real beating put to it. like the sprung ones i've used prior. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT Bastard||07-31-2000||07:23 PM||||Thanks for the info, Travis.  Do you happen to know how much a kevlar disc, bearing, & plate would cost from ACT?  I'm just trying to get an idea.  Too bad I'll be ditching that nice new flywheel that's in there with another one for the 3.2 project. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||07-31-2000||07:42 PM||||OH yeah.. well let me know what you want for the entire current assembly! I'll buy it..  a whole pack from ACT will run about $430.. your best bet what we did with BlackGTs car was ACT disc and Beck Arnley Pressure plate. with matching bearing from NAPA. I'll get you the part numbers... as for JUST the disc i'll call Glenn (Shop manager) in the morning get a part # and call ACT to check on thier "Street Disc" (which is Kevlar unsprung) and let you know.. but you'll pay more for the shiney silver hub than you would if you get the same HUB, i'll check on friction material from <A HREF="http://www.clutchnet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.clutchnet.com</A>  they make the hubs for ACT but ACT puts thier friction material on the other HUB.. I'll check both ways and post in mid-morning. ||||reg||1
